-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart: Ψ(y) spans mathfrak m_S, and Ψ⁻¹(mathfrak m_Sⁿ)=yⁿ
-- statement:
--   **Level and coefficient data.** Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` requires the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise image, under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   **Base ring and chart algebra.** Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with $L$ as its fraction field, such that $q \in \mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the coefficientwise image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion of $j$ (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A K j` $= j$ regarded in $C$. Let $y \subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The integral model.** Let $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-integral chart algebra $C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-integral chart algebra along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with the chart morphism `ιFin` from `XFin A K j` $= \operatorname{Spec} C$ into $X$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-chart package.** For a point $z$ of $X$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of (the image of) $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, and a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin.base y' = z` satisfying the same supersingularity condition as `hss` with $y$ replaced by $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, the package for data $(W,\sigma,f,u,v,e)$ consists of: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ ([`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)) modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v - fu\bigr)$, subject to the following seven clauses, in which $\mathrm{toC}$ denotes the completion map $\mathcal O_{X,z} \to \widehat{\mathcal O}_{X,z}$, $\mathrm{mkS}$ the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY} : C \to \mathcal O_{X,z}$ the map sending $a$ to the germ at $z$ of the corresponding section over the image of the chart `ιFin`:
--   (i) for every $a \in A$, $e$ carries the germ at $z$ of the image of $a$ under `toBase` to the class of the constant $\sigma(a)$;
--   (ii) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), the subalgebra $C$ is stable under $\tau$; here the predicate asserts that for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f_0,g_0$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_{f_0},p_{g_0}$, $p_{g_0}$ giving a nonzero series over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_{f_0}/p_{g_0}$, and every embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has the identity of $q$-expansions $\iota_*\bigl(\tau x\bigr)\cdot \widehat{(g_0\mid_k \delta)} = \widehat{(f_0\mid_k \delta)}$, where $\delta =$ `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix}\gamma^{-1}_{00} & \gamma^{-1}_{01}/q\\ q\gamma^{-1}_{10} & \gamma^{-1}_{11}\end{pmatrix}$;
--   (iii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ as in (ii) preserving $C$, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in y'$ for all $a \in C$;
--   (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'$, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ is compatible with the restriction of $\tau$ under $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$, $\theta$ fixes the classes of constants, $\theta(X_{j_0}) \equiv \sum_{i} M_{ij_0}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij_0} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij_0}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, moreover $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak m_W}$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak m_W}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$;
--   (v) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$, and each containing an element of the form $a_i X_0 + b_i X_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{X,z}$ along $e$ followed by no further map, precomposed with $\mathrm{toC}$, are distinct as soon as $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$;
--   (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ omitting at least one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$ and containing an element $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$: for $a \in C$, the element $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ in $L$;
--   (vii) the function [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with this element minus $a_0$ in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that, for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak m_W$, the value $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\operatorname{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e\bigl(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\text{that element} - a_0))\bigr) = \mathrm{mkS}(h)$.
--
--   **Hypotheses on the package.** The hypothesis `hArig` asserts that for every $z$, $\varpi_z$, $y'$ as above there exist data $(W,\sigma,f,u,v,e)$ satisfying the seven clauses (i)–(vii). In addition, specific data are given: a point $z$ with germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`), and a package $(W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1)$ as above — $W_1$ a complete discrete valuation domain, $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, $u_1,v_1$ units, $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and $e_1$ an isomorphism from $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1 - f_1u_1\bigr)$ — for which the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts the full list of clauses (i)–(vii).
--
--   Finally, an ideal $J$ of $C$ is given together with `hJ`, which requires $J$ to be the infimum of the set of ideals $J'$ of $C$ obtained as follows: $\gamma$ runs over the elements of $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau$ over the $L$-automorphisms of $K$ that are level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of (ii) and preserve $C$, and $J'$ is the contraction along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ of the contraction along $\Psi := e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** With $\Psi : C \to S$ the composite of $\mathrm{germY}$, the completion map $\mathrm{toC}$ and $e_1$, and with $\mathfrak m_S \subseteq S$ the ideal generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi$, $X_0$ and $X_1$:
--
--   1. the ideal of $S$ generated by $\Psi(y)$ equals $\mathfrak m_S$; and
--
--   2. for every natural number $n$, the contraction $\Psi^{-1}(\mathfrak m_S^{\,n})$ equals $y^n$.
--
--   At a supersingular point of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, this identifies the chart map $\Psi$ into the Drinfeld local chart $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1\varpi_t^{q+1}v_1 - f_1u_1)$ as carrying the maximal ideal $y$ onto the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_S$ and matching the $y$-adic filtration with the $\mathfrak m_S$-adic one; it is the version of this comparison for the auxiliary $\Gamma_1(\ell)$ level frame with a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, valid for all primes $q$. It is used in the construction of the isomorphism between the adic completion of a blow-up chart at such a point and its local chart model, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_localChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_localChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd).
